WHAT THIS FORM IS SUPPOSED TO DO:
==============================================
 
This is the CarePath Medical patient registration form for homework 4.
It builds on homework 3 by adding five new features:
 
1. Fetch API - The state dropdown list is loaded from an external
   file called states.html using the JavaScript Fetch API.
   If the fetch fails, a fallback message is shown.
 
2. iFrame - The footer of the page is loaded as a separate
   HTML file (footer.html) using an iFrame tag so it is an
   embedded document inside the main page.
 
3. Sticky Header - The header uses position:sticky in CSS so it
   stays at the top of the screen as the user scrolls down
   through the form.
 
4. Fixed Footer - The footer wrapper uses position:fixed in CSS
   so the footer always stays at the bottom of the viewport.
 
5. Cookies - When the user fills out the form, their first name
   is saved in a cookie that expires after 48 hours. When they
   return to the page, a welcome back message shows their name
   and the first name field is pre-filled. A "Not [name]?" 
   checkbox lets them clear the cookie and start fresh.
   A "Remember Me" checkbox controls whether the cookie is saved.
 
6. Local Storage - All non-sensitive form fields are saved to
   local storage as the user types. When a returning user is
   detected via the cookie, all their previous entries are
   loaded back into the form automatically. SSN and password
   fields are NOT saved to local storage for security reasons.
 
